azgor schrieb:
> 
> This is a collection of YANIs by users of the #nethack IRC channel on
> freenode.net. Please excuse any old ideas that may be present.
> 
> [1]: Silver golems: Just like gold golems, except it's silver. When
> killed, it crumbles into various types of silver equipment. Undead
> avoid them like the plague... or whatever the equivilant of the plague
> is to undead. --TheShrewdDude_

Probably too powerful, unless you make them absurdly rare. They could
provide any amount of the rare and sought silver weaponry, and
allowing armour (shield of reflection) and silver wands[1]/rings could
be
totally silly.

[1] are there silver wands in vanilla NetHack? I know there definitely
are silver rings.

> [2]: The Bank of Yendor: It's where you go to deposit your cash.

Oh dear.

The Bank is a classic YANI and i still haven't seen a good reason for
having one. Next.

> [3]: Swimming skill: Who doesn't want to have a quick refreshing dip
> once in a while?

Not enough water in the dungeon for this to be worth a single skill
slot. Next.

> [4]: when #offering, your god should sometimes grant a wish or a
> (blessed?) genocide in place of an artifact --teabing_

As if there was need for making altar camping more attractive. Next.

> [5]: Zapless condcut. No wands. --SomeoneElseYes

If it only forbids zapping, you can still get wishes, enlightenment
and Elbereth by 'E'ngraving, and in a pinch you can 'a'pply. I haven't
seen much discussion of wandless games so far, so i suspect the demand
for an official conduct of this sort is rather low.

> [6]: Archaeologists should have some sort of bonues against rolling
> boulder traps (Indiana Jones) --ilya86

Perhaps just a special message. Why not? It'd be nicely thematic.

> [7]: kicking a wall should be insta-death by falling boulders and rocks
> --shambler

Erm, how exactly would this add to the game? If you want random
pointless instadeaths, you can always install ADoM and kick a
staircase. 

> [8]: Items should retain their appearance when identified. (ie. i - a
> shiny ring of free action; Q - a mottled spellbook of stone to flesh)
> --TheShrewdDude

Might be provided as an option, but i don't think it would catch on.

> [9]: In real life,

you don't find dungeons filled with magical items. Next.

> [11]: The current dungeons are so terribly boring. Why not have
> -random- levels where there might be a sea (as opposed to checkerboard
> pools), a chasm full of lava, a storm cloud, or an ice area?
> --TheShrewdDude

I think the Dungeon down to the Castle should be kept reasonably
traversible, but that sounds like a good idea for spicing up Gehennom
- might even justify making Gehennom a few levels deeper again.

> [12]: There should also be areas that are date-related.

Friday the 13th and phases-of-the-moon are quite enough influence of
real-world date on the game world for me, thanks. Imagine the Valkyrie
Quest being all one big lake with a few ice floes from June to
September (or from December to April on the southern hemisphere); and
if you go there, save and only restart the game half a year later,
should it all re-freeze in the space of a single game turn?

> [13]: Credit to n54 and Xarann: New conduct: The Counter-Pacifist - You
> must cause conflict throughout the whole game. --TheShrewdDude

Nah. Depends on starting inventory and is thus completely impossible
for most classes. There's no official "Zen" conduct, either.

> [14]: miser conduct: you may not use gold or interact with shopkeepers
> in any way (except as a projectile) --teabing

What's the objective of the conduct and how is it supposed to be
checked? Throwing gold is also a means of payment, btw.

> [16]: When wizards die, Death should visit them. (think diskworld)
> --Botje

The NetHack wizards don't feel like Discworld wizards to me. 

> [18]: The Riders should be able to summon nasties, specifically angels
> and demons. --Thvor

Bleargh. This would make conflict and jumping nearly mandatory on
Astral. For extra suckiness, make them covetous and allow them to
double-trouble you. Fun fun fun.

